{
  "_comment": "Copy to smoke_plan.json and adapt the names/addresses to your instance. phase: read (default) runs always; write runs only with --write and must leave the platform as found (create -> verify -> delete). Steps may capture values from JSON results and reference them as $var in later args. This example assumes devices named PE1/P1/P2/PE2 (TE router-ids 10.0.0.1/.2/.4/.3), a credential profile 'cml-xrd', an SR-PCE provider 'cml-pce' feeding CNC over gRPC with a PCE-delegated SR policy PE1->PE2 color 100, the embedded Data Gateway and the embedded NSO provider; the write phase only touches smoke-* objects, a remove/add mapping cycle that the embedded gateway reverts by itself, and NSO check-sync/sync-from/sync-to on one device.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "tool": "cnc_list_devices",
      "args": {
        "page_size": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_list_devices",
      "args": {
        "page_size": 3,
        "page": 1,
        "response_format": "json"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_list_devices",
      "args": {
        "host_name": "PE*",
        "response_format": "json"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_list_devices",
      "args": {
        "reachability": "reachable",
        "admin_state": "up"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_get_device",
      "args": {
        "host_name": "PE1"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_get_device",
      "args": {
        "host_name": "does-not-exist"
      },
      "expect_error": true
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_get_device",
      "args": {},
      "expect_error": true
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_get_device_collection_summary",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "tool": "cnc_wait_for_device_reachable",
      "args": {
